1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,580
We are about to get REALLY stuck.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:07,860
No beads left to push — not one, anywhere on this rod.

3
00:00:09,120 --> 00:00:11,680
So we carry a bead to the tens rod instead.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:15,560
Let us try nine plus one.

5
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:19,020
First, make nine.

6
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:23,840
Push four lower beads up on the ones rod.

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,340
Now push the upper bead down for five.

8
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:31,880
Four and five together is nine.

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:35,980
Now we want to add one more.

10
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:38,140
But look at the ones rod.

11
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:41,600
Every bead on it is already pushed.

12
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:44,140
There is nothing left to push.

13
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:47,900
So we cannot add one the easy way.

14
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,720
But we are not stuck.

15
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:54,200
There is another rod — the tens rod.

16
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:58,200
The tens rod is empty right now.

17
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:03,420
One bead on the tens rod is worth ten beads on the ones rod.

18
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:09,560
So when the ones rod is full, we carry a bead to the tens rod instead.

19
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:12,600
Here is the clever part.

20
00:01:13,940 --> 00:01:16,160
Some friends do not make five together.

21
00:01:16,840 --> 00:01:18,420
They make ten together.

22
00:01:19,820 --> 00:01:21,520
One and nine are friends.

23
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,400
Two and eight are friends.

24
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,340
Three and seven are friends.

25
00:01:28,080 --> 00:01:30,180
Four and six are friends.

26
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,260
Five and five are friends.

27
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:35,900
Say them with me.

28
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:38,120
One and nine.

29
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:40,340
Two and eight.

30
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:42,760
Three and seven.

31
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:45,240
Four and six.

32
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:47,800
Five and five.

33
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:51,700
These are called the big friends.

34
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,880
Now watch what the friends do.

35
00:01:56,040 --> 00:01:57,620
We wanted to add one.

36
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:00,400
One's friend is nine.

37
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:08,360
So instead of adding one here, we take away nine here, and carry one bead to the tens rod.

38
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:14,860
Because taking away nine, then adding ten, is the same as adding one.

39
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:19,440
It is the same answer, the easy way round.

40
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:22,340
Let us do it.

41
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:26,040
Our ones rod is showing nine.

42
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:29,200
First, we take away nine.

43
00:02:30,340 --> 00:02:34,360
Push the four lower beads down, then push the upper bead up.

44
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:37,780
The ones rod now shows zero.

45
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:40,700
Now, we carry.

46
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:44,760
Push one lower bead up on the tens rod.

47
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,600
That bead is worth ten.

48
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,740
The tens rod shows one.

49
00:02:52,180 --> 00:02:54,020
Nine plus one is ten.

50
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:57,840
We did it, and we never ran out of beads.

51
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:01,960
Let us try eight plus two.

52
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,080
First, make eight.

53
00:03:06,340 --> 00:03:10,260
Push three lower beads up, then the upper bead down.

54
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:12,860
Now add two.

55
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,700
Two's friend is eight.

56
00:03:17,160 --> 00:03:19,900
So first, take away eight from the ones rod.

57
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,100
The ones rod shows zero.

58
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:27,160
Then carry one bead to the tens rod.

59
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,640
The tens rod shows one.

60
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,740
Eight plus two is ten.

61
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,720
Now it is your turn.

62
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,760
Make seven on your own abacus.

63
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,720
Then add three.

64
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:44,660
Three's friend is seven.

65
00:03:45,620 --> 00:03:51,600
So take away seven from the ones rod, then carry one bead to the tens rod.

66
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,500
What number is showing now?

67
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,220
Seven plus three is ten.

68
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,060
Well done.

69
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:05,000
If you enjoyed this video, please like and subscribe for more.

70
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,680
That is your first big friend formula.

71
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:15,680
There is one for every number that needs a friend to reach ten, and we will learn them all.

72
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:20,900
Search for abacus kids on the Apple App Store or Google Play.

73
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:22,720
Download it free.

74
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:27,680
Next time, we will learn all five big friends for adding.

75
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:30,140
See you next time.
